---
title: Protein Balls Without Protein Powder
servings: 36
cuisine: american
main_protein: legumes
prep_time: "30 minutes"
cook_time: "45 minutes"
tags:
  - snack
  - oats
  - peanutbutter
  - hempseeds
  - chocolate
source: https://glutenfreeonashoestring.com/protein-balls/
image: ../obsidian/attachments/Protein-Balls.jpg
leftover_portions: 32
prep:
  - Preheat oven to 300°F if toasting
  - Line a baking sheet with parchment paper
  - Measure out the dry ingredients
---

Optional: Toast oats, coconut, and seeds on a #baking sheet{} at 300°F in the #oven{} for approximately ~{15%minutes}, stirring once, to intensify flavors.

In a #large bowl{}, combine @rolled oats{2%cups}, @unsweetened coconut flakes{1%cup}, @hemp seeds{1%cup}, @oat flour{0.5%cup}, and @kosher salt{0.5%tsp}.

Create a well in the dry ingredients and add @smooth peanut butter{1.5%cups}, @honey{0.5%cup}, and @vanilla extract{1%tsp}. Mix thoroughly and let cool for at least ~{10%minutes}.

Once cooled, fold in @mini chocolate chips{4%oz} to distribute evenly throughout the mixture.

Using an #ice cream scoop{}, portion the mixture into heaping tablespoons onto a parchment-lined baking sheet (approximately 36 portions).

Roll each portion tightly into a ball between your palms.

Refrigerate until firm and serve chilled.
